    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `timezone` field to the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` property to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`PostcodeRegions.java`** \u2014 added the pinned `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneForRegion(region)` lookup returning `null` for unknown regions.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", \u2026)` plus a `timezone(owner)` default method that feeds the owner's existing `locality(owner)` (the region) into `PostcodeRegions.timezoneForRegion`. This keeps `timezone` consistent with `locality`/`customerCode`, and yields `null` when the locality is `UNKNOWN`.\n\nThe test confirms a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) returns `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`.",
